  "observations": {
    "cream": "Warm cream body/head, orange bill and complete shoe uppers, yellow eye ring; dark continuous neck/hip/leg parts and black soles remain readable. The bright footwear is a whole-part finish, not a painted silhouette repair.",
    "graphite": "Gray body/head with yellow bill/shoes and lavender eye ring; dark mechanics retain contrast. No extra band or painted separation was introduced on the body or neck.",
    "lavender": "Lavender body/head, yellow bill/shoes and cyan eye ring are coherent with the saved MicroDuck family. Color follows complete parts and does not add mottled blocks.",
    "sky": "Pale sky body/head with orange bill/shoes and yellow ring; same actual surfaces and camera. Neck highlight bands track the native surface/light, not independent color panels.",
    "board": "Four labels match the individual images; framing, silhouettes, actual seams, sole thickness and visible hardware coincide. Board only rescales and labels the four saved real renders."
  },
  "visible_colour_blocking_defects": [],
  "whole_part_finish_statement": "The dark neck and legs are consistent whole-component mechanical finishes, rather than arbitrary face patches. Pastel main shells, orange/yellow bills and shoe uppers, family-specific eye rings, neutral metal and black rubber preserve the established four-family palette. Native body seams and necessary moving interfaces remain the same as clay 005; color adds no false seams.",
  "scope_limit": "Actually inspected the four supplied oblique color renders and their board. No claim is made to have separately viewed additional rear/sole/inboard color images. Same-geometry neutral 11-view review remains separately scoped in 005. Color images are static actual CAD renders, not deformation or motion evidence.",
